# Conclusion

The application is vulnerable to **Web Cache Poisoning** because arbitrary query parameters influence the generated response without being incorporated into the cache key. An attacker can inject malicious JavaScript into the cached homepage, causing every subsequent visitor to execute attacker-controlled code until the cache entry expires. This significantly amplifies the impact of an otherwise reflected input issue and highlights the importance of ensuring cache keys account for all response-influencing inputs.
